<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jatta National Museum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Museo Nazionale Jatta, Jatta collection</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jatta National Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruvo-di-puglia">Ruvo di Puglia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, displays the collection of ancient vases gathered by the Jatta family in the 19th century from tombs around the town. Its roughly 2,000 objects, mostly Apulian red-figure and Attic painted pottery, are kept in their original arrangement. The best-known piece is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talos">Talos</a> krater, showing the death of the bronze giant Talos.</p></div>
